WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>Uninvited Guests</b>

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.020
Hey! Is anyone there?

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.280
Coming!

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:42.330
I'm sorry, sir, but our restaurant 
doesn't open until the evening.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.510
I know that!

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:49.030
<b>Damian (33) 
A Baron's servant</b>

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:49.020
Tell the owner I want to reserve 
this whole place tonight.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:54.530
I'm very sorry, sir, but I'm 
afraid that's not possible.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:59.930
Girl, I don't think you're head's 
really right for business.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:05.260
The one with the money calls the shots.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.730
I'm terribly sorry.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:07.200
Huh?

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.040
It doesn't matter who it is, our 
place does not have food nor drink

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.480
for someone who wants to have 
the whole place for themselves.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.810
I will interpret those words as an insult!

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.130
You better not come back to me crying!

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:32.120
<i>It's been a while since I've 
been on this particular street.</i>

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:37.010
<b>Gernot (37)
 Tax collector in the ancient city Aitheria</b>

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.610
<i>I'm a little hungry, so this is perfect.</i>

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.720
<i>I'll drop into that place.</i>

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:40.010
<b>Sake</b>

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.760
<i>I want to taste that food overflowing 
with love one more ti— huh?</i>

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:49.940
Baron Brentano, today I really won't hold back.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.530
<i>What's this?</i>

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:53.260
<i>It looks like Baron Brentano is here.</i>

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:56.210
I really don't want to run into them.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.520
Guess I'll come back around next time.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.330
<b>Brentano (41)
  Baron of the Empire</b>

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.740
<b>Eva (14) 
Dishwasher at Nobu. Resident 
of the ancient city Aitheria</b>

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:03.970
I'm sorry.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.590
I'm the one who let them in.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.560
Don't worry about it, Eva-chan.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.820
Thank you for securing this place.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:11.850
It was nothing.

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:15.940
They did make some trouble, but 
this was easy enough for me.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:19.620
Well, then. There is a singular 
reason that I am here today.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.660
At a wedding banquet the other day,

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.600
the bride mentioned the 
name of a certain dish.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:31.310
Something not stinky, not spicy, 
not sour, not bitter, not hard,

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:35.750
not bread, not tubers, not porridge, 
not eggs, and not stew, but delicious.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.460
Ankake yudofu!

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.830
Ankake yudofu?

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.370
That girl.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:52.980
<b>United Kingdom</b>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:52.980
<b>Ancient City</b>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:52.980
<b>Empire</b>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:52.980
<b>La Valicia</b>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:52.980
<b>Eastern Kingdom</b>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:52.980
<b>Old Western Kingdom</b>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:52.980
<b>Holy Kingdom</b>

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:48.530
I am a gourmet who has exhausted the 
culinary delights of the three kingdoms.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:52.990
Therefore, there must not exist
 a delicacy I have not experienced.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:03:00.480
Now, waitress, please bring me 
some of this ankake yudofu.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:06.910
I am terribly sorry, yudofu is something 
we only serve in the winter.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:07.990
What's that?

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.620
You dare to put on airs?!

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.240
Serve it at once!

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:16.000
Yudofu is a dish you enjoy in conjunction 
with the winter cold around you.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.520
I'm afraid this season isn't 
the right time to enjoy it.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.650
Who cares?! You better 
keep your mouth shut an—

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:23.570
Damian.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:28.030
Very well, I will accept what you 
say about the ankake yudofu.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:31.480
If word got around that I made you 
serve a dish not suited to the season,

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.790
it could potentially hurt my reputation.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.800
Thank you.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.610
Still, I am hungry.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.360
I will order something else instead.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.790
A Schnitzel.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:45.830
A Schnitzel?

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.090
What do you say, head chef?

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.540
Can you do that?

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:52.440
Or is that impossible for you foreigners?

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.150
I'll make it.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:56.710
What?

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:00.120
However, we don't normally serve 
this food in our restaurant.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.320
Please allow me some time to prepare.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:04.320
That's fine.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.140
Is that really okay, Taishou?

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.250
Do you actually know what "Schnitzel" is?

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:09.960
No.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.260
But I'm sure if I can find out,
 I can prepare it just fine.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:15.590
Shinobu-chan.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.670
Could you go to the palace guard 
barracks and ask them what that is?

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.280
Taishou, you should go.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.960
Then you can be sure it's right.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:22.890
But...

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.610
I don't want to leave now, 
because it'll feel like a defeat.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.910
Don't worry. If it comes to that, I'll...

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:34.060
Violence is never the answer, Shinobu-chan.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.050
I'll be back soon.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.340
What's that? The chef goes to 
hunt after taking the order?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.570
No, he'll be right back.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.420
Then let's wait for him.

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:51.370
Please, my lord, you're killing me over here.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.790
At this rate I won't be able to eat.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:58.670
Shinobu-san, we're going to be okay, right?

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.040
Don't worry.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.040
Why don't I make you some lunch?

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:03.750
Yes!

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:08.510
We've got the hard-boiled eggs left 
over from yesterday's festival.

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.790
Wouldn't want to waste them, 
so let's use them all.

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:13.530
You're putting in karashi mustard?

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:14.440
Yes.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:19.020
This is karashi mayonnaise and 
it'll make it extra delicious.

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:27.130
Girl, what are you doing over there?

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.900
I'm making this girl something to eat.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:33.440
While your hungry guests are left to wait.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.840
Some establishment this is.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.910
Bring us some of that as well.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.800
This is just a staff meal, 
are you sure you'd like it?

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.370
A baron is telling you 
he is all right with it.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.160
Do not make me repeat myself.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.330
What is this?

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.650
It looks like nothing more 
than bread with filling.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:55.560
That's right.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:58.170
<b>Shinobu's Special Sandwiches</b>

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:58.170
<b>Resisting an egg-salad 
sandwich is impossible.</b>

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:57.160
It's called a sandwich.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.560
Not a name I've heard before.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:05:59.530
Oh, well.

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:01.320
Bring me a knife and fork, then.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.370
You don't need one.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.940
Sandwiches are finger food.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.180
Finger food?

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:06.760
Yes.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.440
They're a great food to 
eat while playing cards.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.370
I see.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.670
Seems like a very plebeian way to eat.

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.650
<b>Soft</b>

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:21.960
Baron Brentano...

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:24.570
Bread as soft as snow.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.830
That faint accent of mustard.

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:31.330
And what is this creamy, rich egg?

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:33.970
I'll have one, too.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:35.340
Me, too!

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:37.780
<b>Soft</b>

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.010
<b>Crunch</b>

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:43.010
<b>Eggy Eggy</b>

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:43.010
That firm but yielding eggy 
texture is irresistible!

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:46.950
<b>Crunch Crunch</b>

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:47.210
The crunch of these vegetables 
don't miss a beat, either!

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:50.000
It's your turn, my lord.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.420
Please have some.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:01.900
<b>Empty empty</b>

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:06.540
Make some more sandwiches, girl.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:09.890
That's fine with me, but 
what about the Schnitzel?

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:12.100
That's something else.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:15.390
I need something more massive 
to fill my stomach first.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:17.040
As quickly as possible.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.300
All right.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.550
Something filling, huh?

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:25.060
I've got it!

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.020
Our special stock of pork fillet.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.170
It's a shame to use up 
something so fancy, but hey.

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:33.420
A customer is a customer.

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:34.740
I've got no choice.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:45.610
<b>Sizzle sizzle</b>

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:48.210
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:52.050
<b>Crackle crackle</b>

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.700
You're up next, sir.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.550
Shh!

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:53.580
<b>Sizzle</b>

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:07.630
<b>Ooze</b>

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:09.560
It's done.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:12.570
<b>Filling sandwich with pork filet cutlet. 
The sauce soaked into the bread is nice, huh?</b>

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:12.570
<b>Shinobu's Special Hirekatsu Sandwich</b>

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.100
My special hirekatsu sandwich.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.580
Please try it.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.800
Hirekatsu sandwich.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:22.910
<b>Crunch</b>

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:23.920
<b>Crunch crunch</b>

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.290
This is...

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.790
This rich sauce...

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.150
This indulgent, crispy, thick-cut meat...

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:38.930
Then, the soft bread holding all the delicious, 
rich flavor of the meat and sauce together.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.440
<b>Fluffy</b>

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:40.080
It's delicious.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.460
This cuisine they call a 
"sandwich" really is delicious.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.290
Thank you very much.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.290
Why don't you try some?

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.510
I-I'm fine, just fine!

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.200
For our food today.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.530
But what about the Schnitzel?

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:00.850
Such irony coming from 
someone with a cute face.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:01.590
Huh?

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:03.500
It was a good meal.

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:05.130
Thank you, Fräulein.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.040
It seems there are many delicacies 
in the world that I do not know yet.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.330
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.320
Get out, you goons!

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.380
We're here for...

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:14.630
Wait, huh?

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:17.110
Shinobu-chan, where is the baron?

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:19.700
They actually left.

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:21.700
B-Baron?!

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:25.220
You mean, the customer who brought 
their goons along was a baron?

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:25.980
Yes.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.200
That was close.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:31.280
We could've been thrown out 
of the ancient city for this.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:33.110
You didn't tell us that, Taishou!

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:36.120
Sorry. I forgot to mention that.

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:40.290
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace guard of city</b>

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:40.290
<b>Hans (23)
 Palace guard of the city</b>

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.170
So now what do we do?

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:40.740
All this tension has dried out my throat!

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.360
Shall we have a drink?

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.730
I'm sorry for all the trouble.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.860
First round's on me.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:49.360
Prosit!

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:56.520
So Taishou, what is Schnitzel?

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.150
Oh, yeah.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.300
It's deep-fried, breaded pork.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.390
So basically, a cutlet.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:04.740
What a coincidence.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.440
We'll have a round of whatsontap.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:08.920
And some karaage.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:09.920
And some edamame.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:10.840
Make that extra!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:12.030
Got it.

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:15.500
It got busy so suddenly.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:19.070
The baron coming in here might 
have been an unexpected boon.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:20.700
Well, then...

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.390
Shinobu-chan, Eva-chan. It's time to work.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:27.810
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:25.130
All right!

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.330
Next up, we have Nobu Plus!

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:33.040
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:42.750
<b>Ochanomizu</b>

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.180
Ochanomizu is an area popular with
 businessmen and students alike.

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:41.270
Back there's the Yushima Seido, in the front 
the St. Nikolai (Holy Resurrection) Cathedral.

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:44.680
Since this bridge connects those two holy 
places, it's called the holy bridge.

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:47.760
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:47.280
We're here in Ochanomizu.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:51.910
You know, I was shocked to find out 
that "Schnitzel" just means "katsu."

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:52.990
I didn't know that.

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:55.170
Katsu. We had that earlier, huh?

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:56.480
Katsu sandwich.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.510
Let's look for one with 
something different in it.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:10:59.590
I know a good place for that!

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:00.810
Nikolai-san!

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:03.180
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the bars

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:05.340
<b>Narrator 
Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.880
here to find the amazing 
dishes featured in "Nobu".

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.810
<b>Nagira Kenichi's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:10.490
The place with the slightly 
different katsu sandwich is here!

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:11.170
Chicken, chicken, chicken.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:11.900
Is this it?

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:12.740
It is.

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:16.650
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi.</b>

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:13.370
Here?

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.380
Oh, here it is.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.170
Looks like it's on the 
second floor. Let's go.

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:23.830
<b>Tokyo Marudori</b>

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:23.830
and its katsu sandwiches.

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.010
Welcome.

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:28.790
So, I was guided here by a divine revelation.

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:29.230
<b>Tokyo Marudori's 
Nozomu Toyoda-san</b>

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:29.220
Right.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:30.790
But I'm wondering if that was a mistake.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:31.620
This <i>is</i> Tokyo Marudori?

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:32.020
Yes.

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.030
It is, sir.

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:35.180
I can highly recommend the roast chicken.

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:36.330
Then I'll take that.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:37.440
Right away, sir.

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:38.760
I don't think this is right.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.740
It's fine, it's fine. Why not
 start off with a whatsontap?

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:44.220
Here's your beer.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:43.920
Thanks.

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:45.680
Where do you roast it?

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:49.500
Over there, you can see our rotisserie 
machines with the chickens in it.

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.030
Oh, those rotating things? Wow!

00:11:50.030 --> 00:11:52.250
It's a slow process to maximize 
the umami concentration!

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:55.180
Here is the Tokyo Marudori. 
Thank you for waiting.

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.970
Nobody eats this by themselves, right?

00:11:58.090 --> 00:11:59.360
Indeed, this looks very filling!

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.210
Once in a while someone does, 
but usually nobody does.

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:04.860
A quarter, or half is more usual.

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:04.110
Of course.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:05.600
But for this occasion...

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.620
Yeah, let's just go for the whole 
thing! Eat it while it's hot!

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:08.660
I guess I'll go for it.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:13.390
It's hot. We finish them 
up at 250 degrees Celsius.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:13.850
That's hot.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:16.990
That's why the outside is so 
crispy, and the inside so juicy.

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:18.690
So? What do you think?

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:20.730
So this is just with salt?

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:23.390
Basically. Salt, garlic, sesame oil.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:25.770
So you can enjoy the chicken itself.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.840
You know it!

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.700
Huh? I think this isn't what 
we're here for today, though.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:32.340
No, remember, it's wedged 
between bread and...

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:34.470
Marudori Style 
<b>Katsu Sandwich</b>

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:33.260
Found it!

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:34.460
Katsu Sandwich!

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:36.560
Is it going to fit after 
I somehow deal with this?

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:41.880
Thick cut chicken breast, fried and 
placed into the bread, then cut!

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:47.020
Thank you for waiting. Here is
 our special katsu sandwich.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.310
Did my heart's voice order this?

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:51.050
Yes, we heard it loud and clear.

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:53.540
Maybe it's the voice of St. Nikolai.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.890
If you'd like, I could bring
 you some wine as well.

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:56.680
Great!

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:58.900
This place is actually also great for wine.

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:01.520
This isn't bread here, this is chicken!

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:02.820
So thick!

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:07.600
We first marinate the meat with 
kiwi to soften it, then we fry it.

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:10.630
"Kiwi" as in the fruit? Not the 
bird that likes cucumbers, right?

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:11.460
No, not that one.

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:12.370
Don't be ridiculous.

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:13.100
So this is extra work.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:13.820
Yes.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:15.400
This is great!

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.170
See?

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:17.490
A chicken trinity.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:19.490
Oh, wrong one. This one.

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:22.080
You're going to finish both anyway.

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:25.300
Even Nagira-san approves 
of this "Tokyo Marudori".

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:27.440
It's a minute walk 
from Ochanomizu Station.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.060
<b>Assistance: Gurunabi                                 To be continued</b>

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:30.170
If you want to have a good katsu 
sandwich, or a whole roasted chicken,

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:31.910
come here. Come here!

